{"rev":13,"ts":"2026-10-29T22:04:23.911242581+00:00","fields":{"__previous_part_content__":"Previous Part: [07](07-native-workflow-switch.md) | Next Part: none\n\n# 08 — Installed real-MCP pilot and acceptance\n\n## Outcome\n\nRun one isolated installed real-MCP pilot from an empty temporary store and no\nprecreated folder, proving the approved native planning lifecycle works across\nrestart and fails visibly rather than falling back to shell chores.\n\n## Non-goal\n\nDo not auto-approve, auto-execute arbitrary work, alter production Missions,\nor treat a fixture pass as a migration of existing archives.\n\n## Inputs and implementation boundary\n\nUse W7's default new-run route. The pilot creates a disposable Session input,\nMission, workspace, plan and approval; it records all returned ids/revisions\nand cleans up only its isolated temporary root.\n\nInstallation/build setup may use the existing installer under a disposable\nprefix. All user-facing intake/planning/lifecycle operations must then use\nthe installed MCP, not hand-authored files or helper shell commands.\nThe requester-decision adapter walkthrough uses an actual requester decision\nfor a harmless pilot plan; automated simulated decisions remain labelled\ntest inputs, never a production grant. Retain the machine transcript and\nmanual decision evidence separately. Missing host support is a failing\nacceptance gate, not permission to accept self-declared actor metadata.\n\n## Expected post-state and validation\n\nThe installed server's named-tool discovery and calls demonstrate: no-folder\nbootstrap; managed workspace lookup; generated plan evidence; rejection before\napproval; exact revision approval; semantic replan invalidation/new approval;\npause/resume; handoff; review-results/add; latest-completion CAS reopen;\nTicket-controlled reopen; restart replay; and explicit errors for unavailable\ninputs/workspace. No manual folder or lifecycle shell command is used.\n\nFuture target: an installed MCP inte